PHYSICAL MAP VALIDITY (asserted, not assumed)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Shipped: physical_map_shortened.json (copy of shortening/physical_map.json).
  - 10/10 devices with real x0/y0/x1/y1, rotation_deg emitted (90 x6, 0 x4),
    mirror emitted (False x10), primitive_cell set on all 10. No nulls.
  - 7/7 nets traced, all "source": "router"; 6 carry segments (Iref legitimately
    has none -- it is internal to the current_mirror_XN5_XN4 macro, and the
    shortening summary independently reports Iref with 0 terminals / 0.00 um).
  - 24 vias total, per net VDD 4 / VSS 4 / Vcont 2 / voutn 5 / voutp 7 / vtail 2 --
    exactly the POST-shortening counts.

  I did NOT run physical_map_from_placement.py, and that is deliberate. The bridge
  reads the canonical routes.json, which is still the PRE-shortening routing
  (total_wire_um = 1397.22, total_vias = 21). Regenerating would have produced a
  map describing routing that no longer exists -- the exact stale-map failure the
  role file warns about -- and route-shortner is not the router, so there is no
  "winning attempt" routes.json to copy over the canonical name. The map built
  from the final geometry is the shortener's own.

  Independently verified rather than trusted, by boolean area comparison of every
  map segment polygon against the flattened GDS:
      vs delivered shortened GDS : 421.68 um^2 of map metal, 0.545 um^2 not present
                                   = 0.129% -- and all 43 residual fragments are
                                   1-116 nm-wide edge slivers (boolean/grid rounding),
                                   not missing wire.
      vs pre-shortening baseline : 130.703 um^2 not present = 30.996% missing.
  So the shipped map describes the delivered geometry and NOT the baseline's.

